// A prelude struct that takes NO type parameters, written with one.
//
// The arity check asks a table of declared parameter counts, and that table
// carried only the GENERIC prelude structs - so for the others it answered "no
// opinion" and the check abstained. "Takes no arguments" is an answer, and
// leaving it unsaid let `Allocator<int>` compile here while the reference
// refused it. No user declaration is involved: this is the prelude's own name,
// applied wrongly, in a program with nothing else in it.
fn takes(x: *const Allocator<int>) { println(1); }

fn main() { println(1); }
